Subject: [PATCH] luci-app-fchomo: drop postinst minimum-version check

The postinst revision check ("Minimum OpenWrt version required is
24.10", r28158) fails on lede snapshots and some 24.10 point releases,
breaking package/install. Remove the check line; the surrounding
REVISION probing becomes inert but is harmless.

Applied to both providers: feeds/small and feeds/kenzok8 (jell).
Converted from Method 3 of the fchomo block in diy-part3.sh via quilt.
(Methods 1-2 target postinst/uci-defaults files that do not exist
upstream and were silent no-ops.)

--- a/feeds/kenzok8/luci-app-fchomo/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/kenzok8/luci-app-fchomo/Makefile
@@ -48,7 +48,6 @@ else
 	REVISION=$$(ubus call system board | jsonfilter -qe '@.release.revision' | cut -f1 -d'-' | sed 's|[a-z]||gi')
 fi

-[ "$$REVISION" -ge 28158 -o "$$REVISION" -eq 0 ] || { 2>&1 echo "Minimum OpenWrt version required is 24.10."; exit 1; }
 # https://archive.openwrt.org/releases/**/version.buildinfo
 # r?????-??????????    25.??.?-rc1
 # r28158-d276b4c91a    24.10.0-rc1
--- a/feeds/small/luci-app-fchomo/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/small/luci-app-fchomo/Makefile
@@ -48,7 +48,6 @@ else
 	REVISION=$$(ubus call system board | jsonfilter -qe '@.release.revision' | cut -f1 -d'-' | sed 's|[a-z]||gi')
 fi

-[ "$$REVISION" -ge 28158 -o "$$REVISION" -eq 0 ] || { 2>&1 echo "Minimum OpenWrt version required is 24.10."; exit 1; }
 # https://archive.openwrt.org/releases/**/version.buildinfo
 # r?????-??????????    25.??.?-rc1
 # r28158-d276b4c91a    24.10.0-rc1
